id: aperture:sophia:number-sense
title: "Sophia / number sense aperture"
kind: aperture
status: draft-0.1
spec_version: aperture.v0.1
updated: 2026-09-09

principal_ref: principal:sophia
guardian_ref: principal:dave
account: "sophie@yawn.yawn.bot"
home: "yawn.bot/sophia"
node_ref: sophia/node.yawn

purpose: >
  The bounded view through which Sophia works on Daddy's computer to learn
  number sense, in the way she asked to learn: by herself, on the real thing,
  with the letters meaning something. Aperture changes visibility and
  salience, not truth or permission (core/projection-and-aperture.yawn).

asked_by:
  who: principal:sophia
  said: "Daddy, can I work on your computer? I want to learn more. I just wanna spell stuff so I can read."
  epistemic_status: reported
  observation_ref: observation:dave:sophia:2026-09-09:can-i-work-on-your-computer
required_by:
  who: "kindergarten assessment"
  what: "counting and cardinality, comparison, compose and decompose within 10, add and subtract within 5"
  epistemic_status: reported
  epistemic_note: "Common Core K.CC, K.OA, K.NBT.1 as Dave understands the school's check; not yet confirmed with the teacher."

teaches:
  - mental-model:dave:number-sense
  - mental-model:dave:prenumerical-thinking

provisioned_to:
  - principal:sophia
  - principal:dave
provisioning_rule: >
  The only way to reach the game is to be provisioned to this aperture. The
  routes are not linked from the hub, are noindex, and are not in the sitemap.
  In the static projection on yawn-ai.github.io the log in button is a local
  stub (a browser-only flag) that stands in for yawn.bot account provisioning;
  nothing leaves the browser. Real provisioning is a yawn.bot account concern.
provisioning_stub_status: assumed

routes:
  - route: what-is-number-sense
    path: "yawn.bot/sophia/number-sense/what-is-number-sense"
    surface: door
    rule: >
      One centered text link, "lacuna", to yawn.bot/lacuna. No expression, no
      aperture, no header, no copy. One account boundary button under it: "log
      in" when out, "log out" when in. When provisioned, one small link to the
      game appears. Nothing else.
  - route: what-is-number-sense/game
    path: "yawn.bot/sophia/number-sense/what-is-number-sense/game"
    surface: game
    rule: >
      The thing she can play to learn what she is being asked to learn. Opens
      with a single "tap to start" (also primes speech). Shows one thing, waits,
      asks. She says the number by tapping it. The game says what it noticed.
      The only ways out are the lacuna link and "leave the game", both behind
      the parent long-press.

notice: >
  Sophia asked Daddy: "Can I work on your computer? I want to learn more. I
  just wanna spell stuff so I can read." Those are her words. Kindergarten will
  check whether she can feel how many, so Daddy made this for her to do by
  herself, on the real computer. It shows one thing. It waits. It asks. She
  taps what she sees, and it says what it noticed. Nobody keeps score, and
  nothing can be lost. Daddy's guess, not her words: she likes to do it herself
  and wants the letters to mean something. If that guess is wrong, she gets to
  say so. It never ends; when she is ready, it adds a little more.

chrome:
  header: "auto-collapses four seconds after the last touch; a thin strip at the top reveals it"
  buttons_on_screen: "the word card (tap to hear), the board, at most three answer cards, LOOK on a covered card"
  navigation: "none for the child; parent settings open on a 1.5 s long-press of the wordmark"
  parent_settings: [voice on/off, level slider, start over, leave the game, lacuna, first-tap rate, peeks, wobbles, a blank line for carry-over]
  tokens: "assets/site.css only; the kid layer is a View over the global tokens"
  color_rule: "color never carries state alone; text, shape, or a spoken word always carries it too"
  never_shown_or_said: [wrong, no, oops, try again, incorrect, a red X, a buzzer, a score, a streak, a timer, a win screen]
  dependencies: none
  storage: "one localStorage key for the level, one for the provisioning stub; nothing leaves the browser"

game:
  design_basis:
    method: "three independent designs (learning-trajectory, one-generator elegance, five-year-old first) judged and grafted"
    winner: learning-trajectory
    epistemic_status: inferred
    epistemic_note: "Proposed by AI from the two models and Dave's brief; Dave verifies; Sophia corrects by what she does."
  principle: "complexity grows by adding structure, never memory. Every round is self-contained. Nothing carries over."
  difficulty:
    state: "one number, level, persisted"
    draw: "60% her edge (newest unlocked skill), 30% review of older skills, 10% a probe of the next skill"
    staircase: >
      Only the first tap of a round is scored. Cold start climbs one per hit until
      her first not-yet; after that two hits up, one not-yet down. Review misses
      are wobbles for the parent, never a demotion. Probes are free. A peek on a
      covered card counts as "counted it": that tap cannot raise the level.
    tail: "beyond level 43 nothing new arrives; the range grows one decade every four levels, forever"
  round_anatomy:
    - show one thing
    - wait
    - ask, with the key word on the word card
    - "she taps; the game says: You said N."
    - "hit: the game says what it noticed and moves on"
    - "not-yet: You said X. Let's look together. Then the modeled count, then the true card rises: Tap N with me. Her tap closes the round: N. There it is."
  answer_cards: "exactly three, ascending, numeral over word; the answer is left, middle, or right with equal chance"
  ladder:
    - at: 0
      key: match
      tier: one for each
      skill_keys: [match, one-to-one, compare, quantity-words]
      mechanic: "plates on top, two trays of cups below; tap the tray with one cup for every plate"
      grows_by: "plates 2 to 6; the wrong tray gets closer (off by 2, then off by 1)"
    - at: 1
      key: compare
      tier: more
      skill_keys: [compare, cardinality, one-to-one]
      mechanic: "two sides; tap the side with more. Aligned rows first, unaligned later, a SAME card from level 16"
      grows_by: "max 3 to 10; aligned to scattered; difference 2 then 1; same allowed"
    - at: 2
      key: pattern
      tier: pattern
      skill_keys: [pattern, sort, order, stable-order]
      mechanic: "a strip repeats a unit; tap what comes next. Shapes differ by shape, never by color alone"
      grows_by: "AB, then ABB or AAB, then ABC"
    - at: 3
      key: sort
      tier: different
      skill_keys: [sort]
      mechanic: "three to four objects, one differs; tap the different one"
      grows_by: "differs by shape, then by size"
    - at: 4
      key: subitize
      tier: just look
      skill_keys: [subitize, cardinality]
      mechanic: "dots appear; after 1200 ms a LOOK cover slides over; how many? A peek re-shows for 1200 ms, always allowed"
      grows_by: "max 3 to 6; dice to scatter; the exposure never shortens"
    - at: 5
      key: one-to-one
      tier: touch and count
      skill_keys: [one-to-one, stable-order, cardinality]
      mechanic: "tap each dot; each tap stamps its numeral and says the next word; then how many?"
      grows_by: "3 to 10; row to scatter"
    - at: 7
      key: size-order
      tier: small to big
      skill_keys: [order]
      mechanic: "three sizes; tap the biggest or the smallest"
      grows_by: "nothing; stays in review"
    - at: 8
      key: make
      tier: make it
      skill_keys: [cardinality, one-to-one, part-whole]
      mechanic: "a number card and empty boxes; tap boxes to fill, tap the number when done"
      grows_by: "row of six, then five frame, then ten frame; n 5 to 10"
    - at: 10
      key: frame
      tier: five frame
      skill_keys: [part-whole, cardinality, subitize]
      mechanic: "five boxes, some filled; how many filled, later how many missing"
      grows_by: "filled to missing"
    - at: 13
      key: invariance
      tier: still the same
      skill_keys: [invariance, conserve, cardinality]
      mechanic: "the game counts n aloud, then they spread; how many now?"
      grows_by: "3 to 8; from level 19 one may visibly come or leave, so always-the-same cannot be gamed"
    - at: 16
      key: order
      tier: number path
      skill_keys: [order, stable-order, count-on]
      mechanic: "a path with one tile missing; what comes after, before, which is missing"
      grows_by: "after only, then before and missing; path from 1, then from k, then 10 to 20"
    - at: 17
      key: fewer
      tier: fewer
      skill_keys: [compare, quantity-words]
      mechanic: "two sides; tap the side with fewer"
      grows_by: "as compare"
    - at: 18
      key: part-whole
      tier: parts
      skill_keys: [part-whole, cardinality, compose-10]
      mechanic: "n in all, a out, the rest under the cup; how many under the cup?"
      grows_by: "5, then 6 to 7, then 10"
    - at: 21
      key: ten-frame
      tier: ten frame
      skill_keys: [part-whole, cardinality, compose-10]
      mechanic: "ten boxes; how many missing"
      grows_by: "as frame"
    - at: 23
      key: add
      tier: some came
      skill_keys: [add-within-5, part-whole, cardinality]
      mechanic: "a dots, then b more come in; how many now?"
      grows_by: "totals within 5, then within 10"
    - at: 26
      key: subtract
      tier: some left
      skill_keys: [subtract-within-5, part-whole, quantity-words]
      mechanic: "n dots, then b fade to ghosts that stay on screen; how many now? all gone when zero"
      grows_by: "totals within 5, then within 10"
    - at: 31
      key: count-on
      tier: count on
      skill_keys: [count-on, cardinality, stable-order]
      mechanic: "a bag shows a numeral; k dots outside; tapping an outside dot says the next word from the bag; how many altogether?"
      grows_by: "bag 3 to 6 with 1 to 3 outside; then bag 10 with 1 to 9 outside"
    - at: 34
      key: teen
      tier: ten and some
      skill_keys: [teen-ten-and-ones, part-whole, cardinality]
      mechanic: "a full ten frame beside some ones; ten and k, how many? Cards light the TEEN chunk"
      grows_by: "ones 1 to 5, then 6 to 9"
    - at: 38
      key: tens
      tier: tens
      skill_keys: [count-by-tens, stable-order, cardinality]
      mechanic: "rods of ten; tapping a rod says ten, twenty, thirty; how many? Cards light the TY chunk"
      grows_by: "1 to 5 rods, then 6 to 10"
    - at: 43
      key: tens-and-ones
      tier: tens and ones
      skill_keys: [count-by-tens, part-whole, cardinality]
      mechanic: "rods of ten and some ones; how many?"
      grows_by: "one more decade every four levels, forever"
    - at: 45
      key: compare-numerals
      tier: which number
      skill_keys: [compare, order]
      mechanic: "two numerals; tap the one that is more"
      grows_by: "range follows the decade"
  reading_bridge:
    rule: "a word is the caption for something she just felt, never the puzzle"
    word_card: "one key word per round, uppercase mono, onset underlined and lit; tap to hear"
    onset: "leading consonant cluster by one regex (TH, SH, ST, TW aware); teen words light TEEN, decade words light TY"
    answer_cards: "numeral over its word, so the numeral, the word, and the felt quantity line up on every hit"
    voice: "browser speechSynthesis, optional; every spoken line is also on screen"
  feedback_language:
    every_first_tap: "You said N."
    hit: ["N. You saw N.", "N. The last word says how many.", "More here. N is more than M.", "Same. One for each.", "Still N. Moved around, still N.", "A and B make N.", "All gone. Zero.", "Ten and K. TEEN."]
    not_yet: ["You said X. Let's look together.", "Tap N with me.", "N. There it is."]
    new_tier: "Let's try a bigger one."
    idle_once: "Tap the dots to count them."

embody:
  - "Ask before assert. The picture comes before the word; the word comes before the answer."
  - "She does; the game narrates. Tapping a dot always counts it. Nothing she taps is wrong."
  - "A not-yet is an observation: it says what she said, looks together, and ends in a hit."
  - "Going bigger is announced; going smaller is silent."

assumptions:
  - text: "She already knows the counting words to ten."
    epistemic_status: assumed
    epistemic_note: "Carried from mental-model:dave:number-sense. If not, levels 0 to 4 are where she sits."
  - text: "Two up, one down keeps her near seventy percent first-tap success, which is her edge."
    epistemic_status: inferred
  - text: "The LOOK cover reads as an invitation, not a timer."
    epistemic_status: assumed
  - text: "Prenumerical moves can be interleaved with counting rather than gated before it."
    epistemic_status: disputed
    epistemic_note: "Piaget versus Gelman and Gallistel, kept visible in mental-model:dave:prenumerical-thinking."

proof:
  signals:
    - "First-tap rate in the parent panel sits near seventy percent and the level climbs across sittings."
    - "She reaches for the dots to count before she taps a card."
    - "She says a number word at the same moment she taps its card."
    - "Away from the screen she says more, same, still five, all gone about real piles."
  falsifier: "If she peeks on nearly every covered card, she is counting, not subitizing; the level drifts down on its own and the tier gets smaller."
  assessment_readiness: "Levels 0 to 34 cover K.CC and K.OA as listed above; level 34 and up cover K.NBT.1 and counting by tens."

lacunae:
  - "Does she know the counting words to ten today?"
  - "Does a level drop ever feel like punishment to her, or is the review pool enough to keep it warm?"
  - "Which speech voices exist on the device she uses, and is voice-off with Daddy narrating the better default?"
  - "Does she show still-the-same before or after she counts reliably?"
  - "Does it carry over: snacks, stairs, socks, with no screen?"
  - "What does the teacher actually check, and when?"

views:
  - sophia/number-sense/what-is-number-sense/index.html
  - sophia/number-sense/what-is-number-sense/game/index.html
validator_ref: scripts/validate-mental-models.mjs
